    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8595" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνηβ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>not yet come to man's
				estate,</i> opp. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔφηβος, παῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Heraclit.
					117
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Leg.Gort.</u>
				11.19
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				14.25
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				8.3
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ἄ.</span>
			<i>pueri</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>CIG</u>
				2034
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Byzantium</span>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				1028.32
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Cos</span>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνηβοι καὶ ἄγονοι ἐκ γενετῆς</span>”
				<i>impotent,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					581b22
				</span></i>
			; of a girl, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				833c
			</span></i>.</div>
